240
00:19:33,661 --> 00:19:36,042
Founded by Harry V.

241
00:19:36,043 --> 00:19:45,820
Wareheim, Hanover Pretzel Company had at the time one product, a soft pretzel.

242
00:19:46,420 --> 00:19:52,140
Growth was slow and steady, but things really took off in the 60s with the purchase of a hard pretzel recipe.

243
00:19:53,060 --> 00:19:58,160
In the early 70s, Michael Wareheim, Harry's grandson and the company's current chairman,

244
00:19:58,840 --> 00:20:02,380
began testing the idea of calling the company's hard pretzel sourdough.

245
00:20:02,381 --> 00:20:11,080
It was really once they named the product Sourdough Hard Pretzels and Mike adopted a box format for packaging the product

246
00:20:11,081 --> 00:20:16,280
that they started to be able to gain distribution really across the United States throughout the 80s.

247
00:20:16,540 --> 00:20:20,720
And it became the country's number one selling pretzels through the mid-90s.

248
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:28,280
Although Snyder's roots can be traced to the early 20th century, pretzels origins go back much further.

249
00:20:28,980 --> 00:20:32,480
We can trace the roots of pretzels back to 610 A.D.

250
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,940
when monks in a monastery in southern France

251
00:20:35,941 --> 00:20:41,580
came up with the idea of utilizing the scraps left over from baking fresh bread.

252
00:20:42,300 --> 00:20:47,660
What he was basically trying to do was create the shape of children's arms folded in prayer.

253
00:20:48,380 --> 00:20:52,120
It was known as a praetiole, Latin for little reward,

254
00:20:52,420 --> 00:20:54,600
and was given to children once they had said their prayers.

255
00:20:55,840 --> 00:20:57,700
It doesn't take much to make a pretzel.

256
00:20:58,280 --> 00:21:03,480
You take some dough, twist it, bake it, and presto, you've got a pretzel.

257
00:21:03,481 --> 00:21:08,400
But what if you wanted to make tons of pretzels an hour?

258
00:21:08,401 --> 00:21:10,640
Over here, we're in our twister section.

259
00:21:10,641 --> 00:21:13,720
This is where we make our sourdough hard pretzels.

260
00:21:13,721 --> 00:21:17,520
We're taking a chunk of dough, putting it in the hopper of this unit.

261
00:21:17,521 --> 00:21:21,320
In this hopper, there's also an auger that extrudes out a dough ball.

262
00:21:21,321 --> 00:21:23,840
It's rolled out between a series of rollers.

263
00:21:23,841 --> 00:21:28,820
Once we get a noodle roll, there's two mechanical fingers that actually hand-tie the pretzel.

264
00:21:29,400 --> 00:21:34,160
That takes us from maybe 100 pounds an hour that might have been expected in the 30s

265
00:21:34,161 --> 00:21:36,400
when this first automation hit the category,

266
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:40,900
to today where we'll produce in many of these ovens over 2,000 pounds an hour.

267
00:21:42,220 --> 00:21:46,220
It'll take between 7 and 15 minutes for these pretzels to reach the oven.

268
00:21:46,660 --> 00:21:50,000
During that time, yeast converts fermentable sugars in the dough

269
00:21:50,001 --> 00:21:54,600
into the leavening gas, carbon dioxide, causing the dough to rise.

270
00:21:56,140 --> 00:21:57,740
You're doing two things in an oven.

271
00:21:58,140 --> 00:22:03,300
You're baking in the top zone, and in the bottom zone of the oven is a kiln or dry zone.

272
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:09,300
During the baking process, you're also developing flavor and aroma at that point in time.

273
00:22:10,240 --> 00:22:15,180
Once you get to the end of the oven, you drop your product into a kiln zone, which is a drying zone.

274
00:22:15,181 --> 00:22:23,020
The pretzels, which started with between 46 and 48 percent moisture, have had that baked

275
00:22:23,021 --> 00:22:28,560
down to between 16 and 19 percent in the top of the oven.

276
00:22:28,561 --> 00:22:33,940
In the bottom kiln zone, that will drop to between 4 and 5 percent.

277
00:22:33,941 --> 00:22:41,880
Then the pretzels will be cooled, packaged, and palletized, stacked on pallets, to be

278
00:22:41,881 --> 00:22:47,380
shipped to markets in Europe, the Middle East, Asia, Pacific Rim countries, and North and

279
00:22:47,381 --> 00:22:51,640
South America. Efficiently marketing to the world begins here.

280
00:22:51,641 --> 00:22:54,892
This palletizing unit was installed in August of 2002.

281
00:22:54,893 --> 00:22:57,060
It was a capital investment of close

282
00:22:57,061 --> 00:23:01,020
to two and a half million dollars, and we clearly had the good justification to pay

283
00:23:01,021 --> 00:23:04,493
that back from a labor efficiency within a couple years.

284
00:23:04,494 --> 00:23:06,540
The system is capable of handling

285
00:23:06,541 --> 00:23:11,860
about 45 to 60 cases per minute. In a lot of cases, that may translate into about 25

286
00:23:11,861 --> 00:23:13,860
to 28,000 cases per shift.

287
00:23:14,820 --> 00:23:15,920
Snyder's has expanded

288
00:23:15,921 --> 00:23:17,800
into organic

289
00:23:17,801 --> 00:23:19,780
pretzels and over 30 different

290
00:23:19,781 --> 00:23:21,820
varieties of pretzels, flavors, shapes

